# UI / design system

Stack: **Tailwind v4** (PostCSS plugin), **Radix UI** primitives, **Framer Motion** for motion, **lucide-react** for icons, **sonner** for toasts, **TipTap** for the editor, **dnd-kit** for drag-and-drop, **Recharts** for charts. Fonts: Inter (sans + mono), Oswald (display).

## Token system (single source: `src/app/globals.css`)

Re-skin the entire app by changing four knobs:

```css
--revint-h:   38;   /* hue 0–360 — current: warm ochre/orange */
--revint-s:   78%;  /* saturation */
--revint-ns:  7%;   /* neutral surface saturation */
--revint-nts: 10%;  /* neutral text saturation */
```

Everything below derives from those:

- Primary scale: `--revint-100` ... `--revint-900` (HSL, lightness step ramp)
- Surfaces: `--revint-bg`, `--revint-surface`, `--revint-card`, `--revint-hover`, `--revint-border`
- Text: `--revint-text-1` (primary), `--revint-text-2` (secondary), `--revint-text-3`, `--revint-muted`
- Semantic: `--revint-success`, `--revint-warning`, `--revint-error`, `--revint-info`
- Glow: `--revint-glow-soft`, `--revint-glow-medium`, `--revint-glow-strong`

**Legacy tokens map onto the leadac scale**:
- `--system-blue/green/orange/red/purple/teal/yellow` (iOS dark mode names — kept for backward compat)
- `--label-primary/secondary/tertiary/quaternary` (text alpha ramp)
- `--shadow-sm/card/elevated/modal`
- `--border-primary/light`, `--separator`, `--separator-opaque`

**Cinematic palette** (only used by `src/components/marketing/cine/*`):
- `--cine-ink`, `--cine-cream`, `--cine-ochre`, `--cine-terra`, `--cine-indigo`, `--cine-border`, `--cine-gutter`, `--cine-max`

`src/lib/colors.ts` (`REVINT_HUE` / `REVINT_SATURATION`) MUST stay in sync with the CSS knobs.

## Tailwind v4 — what's different

- Use `@import "tailwindcss"` in the CSS entry point (we do, see `globals.css`).
- Theme extension is via `@theme inline { ... }` — see `globals.css` for `--color-*`, `--font-*`, `--animate-*`.
- No `tailwind.config.js`. Customisations go in `globals.css` with `@theme`.
- Class arbitrary values still work: `bg-[var(--revint-card)]`, `text-[hsl(var(--revint-h)_var(--revint-s)_50%)]`.
- Use `cn()` from `src/lib/utils.ts` (clsx + tailwind-merge) for conditional classes.

## Component conventions

- **Primitives** live in `src/components/ui/` (Button, Card, Dialog, Dropdown, Input, Select, Tabs, Tooltip, Badge, Separator, Progress, Skeleton, Textarea, Toaster, ScrollArea, Popover, Label, Slot). All wrap a Radix primitive or a Tailwind-styled element. Variants via `class-variance-authority`.
- **Product surfaces** live in `src/components/app/`. They consume `ui/` primitives.
- **Marketing surfaces** live in `src/components/marketing/`. Cinematic landing in `marketing/cine/*`.
- **Server vs client**: components default to server. Only add `"use client"` when you need state, effects, refs, framer-motion, or browser APIs. Pass server-fetched data into client components as props.

## Brand colors — DO NOT hardcode

```tsx
// ✅ token references
<div className="bg-[var(--revint-card)] text-[var(--revint-text-1)] border border-[var(--revint-border)]" />

// ✅ semantic
<span className="text-[var(--revint-success)]" />

// ❌ hex / rgb literals
<div className="bg-[#1a1a1a] text-white" />
```

Brand source files: `public/logo.png`, `public/leadac-brand-kit.pdf`, `public/brand-kit.html`.

## Motion

- Use Framer Motion for view-level entrances (hero blur-up, marquees, drawer slides).
- Existing keyframes in `globals.css`: `marquee`, `marquee-rev`, `cine-blur-up`, `cine-drift`.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — wrap any non-decorative animation.

## Glass / liquid

`.glass` and `.glass-strong` utilities (in `globals.css`) handle `backdrop-filter` correctly across browsers. Don't reinvent — reuse.

## Mobile / safe area

iOS notch utilities: `.safe-pt`, `.safe-pb`, `.safe-pl`, `.safe-pr`, `.safe-mt`, `.safe-mb`. Form inputs auto-bump to `font-size: 16px` under 640px to block iOS auto-zoom.

## i18n

Bilingual TR/EN content lives in `src/i18n/`. Marketing surfaces support both via `lang` segment. When adding marketing copy that ships in both languages, also update the TR variant — see the `tr-en-marketing-sync` skill for the workflow.

## Icons

`lucide-react` only. Don't import emoji-as-icon. Use 16/20/24 px sizes (`<Icon className="h-4 w-4" />`).

## Charts

`recharts` for in-app analytics dashboards. Theme via `--revint-*` tokens — pass `stroke="var(--revint-500)"` style.

## Anti-patterns

- ❌ Hardcoded hex/rgb/named colors in JSX — use `--revint-*` / `--system-*` tokens
- ❌ Adding a `tailwind.config.js` — Tailwind v4 doesn't use one here
- ❌ Inline `<style>` blocks for one-off styling — extend `globals.css` if it's a real pattern
- ❌ Client component for static content — keep it server unless you need interactivity
- ❌ Importing icon SVGs from public/ when `lucide-react` already has it
